cff-version: 1.2.0
title: PARAPET
message: >-
  If you use PARAPET, please cite the software and the papers its
  components implement.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Zhao
    given-names: Yutong
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9307-5532"
    affiliation: California State University, Long Beach
  - name: The PARAPET Authors
repository-code: "https://github.com/Yutong0711/PARAPET"
license: Apache-2.0
abstract: >-
  PARAPET turns a security or performance exposure into a reviewable
  decision: it classifies the exposure, measures what a candidate fix
  costs at run time, reports where in the architecture that cost lands,
  and checks the result against a service budget the maintainer declared
  in advance. The output is a hardening record.
keywords:
  - software performance
  - software architecture
  - supply chain security
  - issue triage
